{"runs":[[0,4,0,"v1 and v2 Firestore create triggers use distinct registration bodies and dispatch exact legacy-event and CloudEvent envelopes to the Functions emulator"],[4,1,0,"v1 and v2 Firestore create triggers use distinct registration bodies and dispatch exact legacy-event and CloudEvent envelopes to the Functions emulator"],[5,7,1,"Callable and HTTP functions: envelopes, typed errors and unknown functions"],[12,2,1,"Functions discovery at startup and after a source change"],[14,6,2,"Functions startup: inventory and trigger records"],[20,2,2,"Registration with the auxiliary emulators at startup"],[22,3,3,"GET /backends after readiness: every codebase, the static manifest, the broken codebases and the local extension backend."],[25,7,3,"404 bodies for an unknown function id (lists every registered trigger key), an unknown region, an unknown project and an unknown path."],[32,6,3,"Explicit and multi-region deployments answer on their region path only."],[38,9,3,"Secondary, ESM and static-manifest codebases serve; the broken and invalid-dotenv codebases export nothing."],[47,3,3,"A Realtime Database export is discovered but ignored; its trigger route still exists. The task-queue export registers with the Tasks emulator."],[50,13,3,"Every HTTP method reaches the v2 onRequest handler; the handler records url, path, query, headers, ip and body parsing."],[63,8,3,"Sub-paths, query strings, trailing slashes, encoded characters and dot segments under the function route."],[71,8,3,"Status codes, custom headers, redirects, empty bodies, text bodies and chunked streaming responses pass through the proxy."],[79,6,3,"Synchronous throw, asynchronous rejection, throw after headers, a handler that never responds, and a per-function timeout."],[85,8,3,"SDK-level CORS on onRequest({cors}) for preflights and simple requests with allowed, disallowed and absent origins."],[93,4,3,"First-generation https.onRequest, region and runWith options on the secondary codebase."],[97,2,3,"The